- The other half is in real danger. An open Supabase bug (created 2026-09-20, last updated 2026-11-05) makes the consent step return 400 on any of three triggers: a public client, the offline_access scope, or the RFC 8707 resource parameter. Claude's documented flow sends resource unconditionally and requests offline_access whenever the server advertises it, which this project's live metadata does. Pre-registering a confidential client avoids only one of the three triggers. If that bug still reproduces, the falsifier's flow-failure clause is met and S7 needs its own OAuth layer.
- Prerequisite found: the OAuth server is disabled on the live project right now (public discovery endpoint returns feature-disabled). Enabling it is a dashboard action only Dennis can take.
